   369	/**
   370	 * idn2_lookup_u8:
   371	 * @src: input zero-terminated UTF-8 string in Unicode NFC normalized form.
   372	 * @lookupname: newly allocated output variable with name to lookup in DNS.
   373	 * @flags: optional #idn2_flags to modify behaviour.
   374	 *
   375	 * Perform IDNA2008 lookup string conversion on domain name @src, as
   376	 * described in section 5 of RFC 5891.  Note that the input string
   377	 * must be encoded in UTF-8 and be in Unicode NFC form.
   378	 *
   379	 * Pass %IDN2_NFC_INPUT in @flags to convert input to NFC form before
   380	 * further processing.  %IDN2_TRANSITIONAL and %IDN2_NONTRANSITIONAL
   381	 * do already imply %IDN2_NFC_INPUT.
   382	 * Pass %IDN2_ALABEL_ROUNDTRIP in @flags to
   383	 * convert any input A-labels to U-labels and perform additional
   384	 * testing (not implemented yet).
   385	 * Pass %IDN2_TRANSITIONAL to enable Unicode TR46
   386	 * transitional processing, and %IDN2_NONTRANSITIONAL to enable
   387	 * Unicode TR46 non-transitional processing.  Multiple flags may be
   388	 * specified by binary or:ing them together.
   389	 *
   390	 * After version 2.0.3: %IDN2_USE_STD3_ASCII_RULES disabled by default.
   391	 * Previously we were eliminating non-STD3 characters from domain strings
   392	 * such as _443._tcp.example.com, or IPs 1.2.3.4/24 provided to libidn2
   393	 * functions. That was an unexpected regression for applications switching
   394	 * from libidn and thus it is no longer applied by default.
   395	 * Use %IDN2_USE_STD3_ASCII_RULES to enable that behavior again.
   396	 *
   397	 * After version 0.11: @lookupname may be NULL to test lookup of @src
   398	 * without allocating memory.
   399	 *
   400	 * Returns: On successful conversion %IDN2_OK is returned, if the
   401	 *   output domain or any label would have been too long
   402	 *   %IDN2_TOO_BIG_DOMAIN or %IDN2_TOO_BIG_LABEL is returned, or
   403	 *   another error code is returned.
   404	 *
   405	 * Since: 0.1
